  "contracts": [
    "DataflowEquations describes only operations actually read by the worklist and the integer liveness model; it does not copy a driver interface or invent registry membership.",
    "Compact specialization keeps exact class/method identity guards, decoded observation copies, actual map identities and customized-analysis fallback. Erased fallback facts are not asserted to have an arbitrary Fact type.",
    "DefUse now calls the real Dataflow driver with dependency arguments, reads published block-entry maps, decodes actual IRStatement facts and applies the preceding statement prefix. It returns and publishes the same public (stores, loads) tuple.",
    "Reaching definitions retain a compound statement while any written target survives. Single-target kills stay exact; compound statements can remain conservative extra witnesses for overwritten names.",
    "Entry templates keep malformed runtime IR as an explicit uncovered value despite nominal field types; ordered shape/origin sorting is unchanged.",
    "Actual AST residual metadata is finite-checked, preserves exact immutable tuple identity and uses the host iteration protocol exactly once for other payloads.",
    "IR Import metadata remains absent until the real resolver writes it. IRYield.get_ast returns the actual Expr/Assign wrapper rather than incorrectly claiming the inner Yield expression.",
    "Liveness/CFG constructor changes are actual annotations. Initial CFG constructor-port plus formatting AST equivalence is retained; subsequent star-import cleanup preserves the existing graph/edge algorithms and explicitly re-exports NormalEdge."
  ],
